      "where": "fetch layer",
      "impact": "Every fetch is a full request - sessionId 0, sessionEpoch -1, an empty forgotten-topics list - so a poll re-sends every assigned partition rather than only what changed. This is a decision, not an oversight: 3.0.0 ships sessionless (decision D31), and the three fetch-session error codes are mapped defensively so an unexpected one cannot crash a consumer. Incremental fetch is the prerequisite for reducing request size on a large assignment.",
